1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,480
Hi, I'm Tom from the Burp Scanner development team. Today I'm going to talk a little bit about

2
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:11,440
Incy Wincy mode in Burp Scanner. So we're continually adding features to Burp Scanner

3
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:15,680
so that it can increase coverage when crawling the modern web, especially when there are behaviors

4
00:00:15,680 --> 00:00:20,400
that make crawling otherwise difficult. But some web applications are actually really easy to crawl,

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,320
and we don't necessarily want all of these bells and whistles turned on if they come at their cost

6
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:30,480
of performance. So how does Incy Wincy mode differ from the default crawling settings? There are three

7
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:34,960
main ways I'm going to go over using Portsfugger's Gin and Juice Shop to do some manual examples.

8
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:42,320
So the first way in which they differ is path walking. By default when Burp Crawler is running,

9
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:46,640
what it'll do is if it's on a page it will record all the links it sees as well as where it's seen

10
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:52,000
them and then walk back to where it saw each link before following it. This means that it makes sure

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,160
that it's always got the same session as when it saw a link to make sure it'll be there when it goes

12
00:00:56,160 --> 00:01:01,360
back again. So if we have this page for example, the products page in Gin and Juice, it's got all

13
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:09,280
these product links. What it would do is effectively put the Gin and Juice Shop address in the address bar

14
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:13,760
and go to the products page and click on product one and put the Gin and Juice Shop address in the

15
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:20,080
address bar again, go to products, go to product two and so on and so forth. How Incy Wincy mode differs is

16
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:24,800
instead of maintaining a list of paths, it just maintains a list of URLs that it scraped off the

17
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:29,920
page. So again, if it was on this product page and it saw all of these product links, what it would do

18
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:35,760
is just record the URLs and paste them into the address bar directly. So it would first go to product

19
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:42,240
one and then it would put product two in the address bar and product three and so on. This is pretty much

20
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:47,520
exactly how Burp Spidey used to work and is where unsurprisingly the name Incy Wincy comes from.

21
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:53,440
The second way in which it differs is the use of Burp Suites built-in cookie jar. So because by

22
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:58,000
default the crawler is trying to create and maintain sessions itself, it doesn't interact with Burp's

23
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:03,200
cookie jar at all. Incy Wincy mode on the other hand does. When it starts up, it'll take a copy of

24
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:07,760
all the cookies in the cookie jar and use those as a starting point for crawling. This is useful if you

25
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:13,200
want to use Burp Suites embedded proxy to authenticate and then have the crawler continue to use your

26
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:20,240
authentication, assuming it's cookie based. So for example, you could use Burp's proxy to go and log in

27
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:28,960
and then go and kick off a crawl using Incy Wincy mode and it would just continue crawling using this

28
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:35,760
this session. The caveat here is that again similar to the Burp Spidey of old, you have to make sure to put

29
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:43,600
any session killing links out of scope because Incy Wincy mode will, for example, see this logout link,

30
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:48,160
follow it and then just barrel on without noticing that it's lost its authenticated session.

31
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:51,440
Authentication is also the third way in which

32
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:58,800
the Incy Wincy mode differs from the default crawl settings, this time with automatic authentication.

33
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:05,440
So the way in which the default crawler handles authentication is in separate phases. Firstly,

34
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:10,400
the crawler will do one phase completely unauthenticated, making a note of any login forms

35
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:16,240
it finds along the way. It'll then do a follow-up pass where it goes back to these login forms and

36
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:22,240
uses any credentials you've given it to log in and crawl from there. So it would crawl like this

37
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:27,680
without any authentication, spot this login form and then in the follow-up pass it would go and fill that

38
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:33,440
out and crawl from there. The behavior is the same with recorded logins in that it'll do one pass without

39
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:36,800
any recorded logins you've given it and then it'll do a follow-up with those recorded logins and kind

40
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:41,520
of compare what it sees to what it saw when it was unauthenticated. Incy Wincy on the other hand does it

41
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:47,200
all in one go. So if you've given it any recorded logins it will just start with those or do them very

42
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:52,080
early on in the crawl and if it spots any login forms along the way it'll just fill them out as it

43
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:58,000
sees them rather than waiting to do them in a follow-up pass. So finally I'll hop over to Burp

44
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:06,320
Suite and just show you how to turn this on. So if we go to a custom crawl configuration and go to the

45
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:12,320
crawl optimization, Incy Wincy mode is actually on by default if you select the fastest crawl settings.

46
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:17,680
That's because we intended the fastest settings to work on or be used on the same kind of websites we

47
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:23,200
think Incy Wincy mode will work best on. So ones that don't use too many modern or difficult to crawl

48
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:29,680
behaviors. If you want to combine Incy Wincy mode with your own custom configuration you can manually

49
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:37,760
enable it or disable it inside these settings here. We added Incy Wincy mode or specifically the ability

50
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:46,880
to crawl favoring speed over thoroughness as a result of users asking for it. So if you have any more

51
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:52,400
ideas keep them coming.

